[list]
[*]New: a stand can serve a radius or an allowed area instead of its room. Choose under Serves, at the bottom of the stand's settings. Within a radius covers every cell within a set distance of the stand, from 3 to 79 cells, walls or no walls, and draws the ring while the stand is selected. An allowed area covers whatever you paint. The menu lists your areas with their colours, New allowed area starts one from the stand's room, and Paint and Manage areas open vanilla's own tools. The stand has to stand inside its area. A shed in the fields, a fishing hut on the shore, a cell block or a build site can each have its own uniform now.
[*]Inside a radius or an area, the uniform stays on for what the stand serves, and for idling and wandering. At a work stand it also stays on for hauling, cleaning and building where every place the job names is inside. Most other jobs change them back first, a sit-down meal or work the stand does not serve among them. A sleep stand is stricter: pyjamas stay on only in bed, and on the way to a bed inside its ring or area.
[*]Changed: a stand standing in the open and serving its room now serves nothing, work included. Every outdoor cell belongs to one map-wide room, so a work stand there used to dress colonists for every outdoor job on the map. A new alert, "Shift stand serves nothing", lists those stands: give them a radius or an allowed area under Serves. A walled but roofless yard is its own room and works as before.
[*]The same alert lists a stand whose allowed area has been deleted, or that stands outside its area. It serves nothing until you choose again, rather than falling back to its room, and a new area under the old name is not adopted. A gravship landing is the exception: a stand on the deck is bound again to the area painted there.
[*]Changed: fetching building materials, a tree to replant or seeds to plant no longer dresses anyone. A builder whose stand serves construction keeps the hardhat on for it, and a gardener whose stand serves growing does the same for a tree or seeds, as long as every site the load goes to is inside the stand's room, ring or area. The job starts at the stack, so a builder used to change for the walk to the stockpile, or change out before it. The hardhat now goes on at the frame. A stand serving an allowed area that covers both the stack and the site is the exception, and dresses the builder before the first load, unless they rank hauling above construction. In pyjamas or another stand's outfit, the outfit stays on only if the whole trip, stockpile included, is inside.
[*]Fixed: a colonist in pyjamas, or without the armor they parked overnight, carried a meal to a patient or a prisoner as they were. They change back first now, unless the whole trip stays inside the stand's room. A doctor's, a handler's or a warden's uniform still stays on for it while the patient or prisoner is inside the stand's room, ring or area.
[*]Fixed: ticking Fishing did nothing. Odyssey hands fishing out differently from other work, so no stand ever saw it. A stand ticked for Fishing now dresses for it, and a fishing hut serving a radius that covers the shore was the missing setup.
[*]Fixed: with Medical emergencies change first off, a colonist in uniform who needed a doctor urgently, with their bed outside the stand's room, went to the stand to change back before lying down. They now go straight to bed, and a bedroom stand no longer stops them for sleepwear on the way.
[*]Fixed: a stand beside a door could dress a colonist for work on the door or in the doorway, such as repairing the door, then send them back to change for that same job. A stand now serves only work in its own room.
[*]Fixed: a colonist in uniform sent to rescue a baby left somewhere unsafe, outside the stand's room, stopped at the stand to change first. A rescue now goes straight to the baby.
[*]Changed: Change back holds at the stand they changed back at, and at any stand serving the same thing whose room, radius or area takes that stand in, rather than at every stand in the room. It also lifts once they have slept, as well as when they leave.
[*]Changed: the job a colonist was just dressed for no longer sends them straight back to change when its target moved while they changed, such as an animal that wandered out of the barn.
[*]Every stand still starts on This room.
[/list]
